 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? The simple and cheap option is cable ties. You can wrap them around the cables and desk so they can move freely but the cables themselves can't wrap. No problem. The simple and cheap option is cable ties. You can wrap them around the cables and desk so they can move freely but the cables themselves can't wrap. Very easy. You pop the cables through holes in the desk, loop the cable ties around, and tighten the little clip. It works best on straight and simple paths, so it's worth trying on the laptop charger next. You can tape a small piece of card with a label on it off the end, so you see which way it goes. Push it through and fold the end back on itself.",
